  "notes": "{降|お}ろす is a transitive godan verb meaning to take down, unload, or withdraw.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{降|お}りる→降りる：00568_oriru⟧ (intransitive, to get off/descend)\n\nWRITING:\n- {降|お}ろす: unload, drop off (people/cargo)\n- ⟦{下|お}ろす→下ろす：02029_orosu⟧: lower, take down (general)\n- ⟦{卸|おろ}す→卸す：02463_orosu⟧: wholesale (different word)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{荷物|にもつ}→荷物：00737_nimotsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{降|お}ろす: to unload luggage\n- ⟦{客|きゃく}→客：00865_kyaku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{降|お}ろす: to drop off a passenger\n- ⟦{棚|たな}→棚：01650_tana⟧⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧{降|お}ろす: to take down from a shelf\n- ⟦{お金|かね}→お金：00611_okane⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{降|お}ろす: to withdraw money\n- ⟦カーテン→カーテン：01342_kaaten⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{降|お}ろす: to lower the curtain\n\nUSAGE:\nFor withdrawing money, both {降|お}ろす and ⟦{下|お}ろす→下ろす：02029_orosu⟧ are used. The {降|お}ろす kanji emphasizes 'bringing down' from a higher place (like an account).",
